From 5fd7b28b939d9aff5497cab1ac5f3a87cc19a687 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:08:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 84/98] pvr: keep the pixels around a partial render area of a
 TFBC image

The PBE store of a TFBC attachment writes whole 8x8 blocks, so with a
partial render area the pixels around the area have to be loaded first.
The force-load variant of a render's load op only covered the
attachments in color_init, and DONT_CARE attachments never got an entry,
so their pixels in the edge blocks were lost (renderpass1/2
suballocation.attachment cases once their images were compressed).

Render passes now give DONT_CARE attachments that could be TFBC images a
render init entry. The normal load op leaves them alone: it is only
created when an entry does initialize something, and the background
object and empty tile processing count only initialized entries. Dynamic
rendering promotes DONT_CARE and NONE to LOAD for a TFBC image with a
partial render area.

Also:
- clears at the start of a render looked up the init entries of hardware
  render 0 whatever the current render was, reading past its color_init
  for a later render (crash in pvr_clear_attachments from
  vkCmdNextSubpass2);
- pvr_loadops_contain_clear() indexed color_init up to count squared.

CTS: TFBC list (9170) identical to before, both alone and with TFBC for
sampled, input attachment and transfer destination images, where the
other lists (render pass load_store_op_none/attachment_allocation/
render_area sample, TFBC copy/clear sample, dynamic rendering, 5062,
loops/indexing/graphicsfuzz, synchronization, robustness) are identical
too.
